// 26 U.S.C. §§6103, 6104, 6105, 6110 — Confidentiality and Disclosure of
// Returns and Return Information (F01c, IRC-15). The text is pinned whole
// (`sources.law`, generated by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irc_fragments.py --package confidentiality` from
// the shared Title 26 snapshot, docs/foundations/us-irc/SOURCE-MANIFEST.json).
//
// STAGE 1 SCOPE (this agent's task; full list and rationale in
// docs/foundations/us-irc/coverage/confidentiality.json and the final
// report):
//   FULL:    §6103(a) general prohibition (all three bearer classes),
//            §6103(b)(1)-(4) definitions used by this stage's rules,
//            §6103(c) designee of taxpayer, §6103(d)(1) State tax
//            officials, §6103(f)(1) committees of Congress (closed-
//            session/consent condition), §6104(d)(1)-(2),(4) public
//            inspection duty with exact 30-day/immediate windows and the
//            widely-available exception, §6105(a)-(b)(1),(2),(4) treaty
//            confidentiality, §6110(a),(g)(1)-(2) written-determination
//            timing.
//   PARTIAL: §6103(e) material interest (individual, joint-return spouse,
//            >=1% shareholder, (e)(7) return information only — not the
//            full (1)(C)-(F)/(2)-(6)/(8)-(11) list), §6103(p)(3)(A)/(4)
//            safeguards and recordkeeping (consolidated duties, not each
//            (A)-(E) condition separately), §6110(b)-(c) definitions and
//            deletion categories (classification only, not a per-document
//            `must_delete` computation).
//   Everything else among this package's 930 dispositions (§6103(g)-(q)
//   except (p) as above, §6103(d)(2)-(6), §6103(e) remainder, §6104(a)-(c),
//   §6105(b)(3), §6110(d)-(l) except (g)(1)-(2)) is `unreviewed`,
//   `EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY`, `NON_NORMATIVE` (statutory notes), or `TECH_GAP`
//   per the coverage rows — see the final report for the classification
//   of each and what a next stage should build first.
//
// JUDGMENT CALLS AND GAPS (see report for the full list):
//  - §6103(a)(2)/(3)'s bearer classes are modeled as direct case facts
//    (`state_officer_with_access`, `other_person_with_access`) rather than
//    derived from each cross-referenced subsection's own access grant —
//    module 00 header explains why.
//  - §6103(b)(4) "tax administration" purpose is one empirical case fact
//    per disclosure, not a further-decomposed classification of its
//    (A)(i)-(ii)/(B) list.
//  - §6103(b)(5) "State" covers only the core 50-states/DC/territories
//    list, not the municipality/regional-income-tax-agency extension
//    (needs decennial-census population data this package cannot pin).
//  - `us.irc.exempt_organizations` is still a package skeleton (no `pub`
//    symbols as of 25.09.2026): §6104(d)'s `described_501c_or_d_or_527a`
//    is a local placeholder pending that package's `exempt_organization`
//    export (recorded in `coverage/confidentiality.deps.json`).
//  - §6110(g)(1)(B)'s "if later" comparison against the (g)(1)(A) 90-day
//    date is NOT computed (no `max`-over-derived-dates primitive used) —
//    module 08 header.
//  - `unauthorized_disclosure(d: Disclosure)` is PUBLISHED for
//    `judicial-proceedings` (§7431 civil damages) to import once that
//    package is ready to state the dependency as resolved rather than
//    EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (its own package is still mid-write as of this
//    stage). `committee_written_request`/`chairman_of_committee` (module
//    04) similarly stand ready for `joint-committee`'s §8021(a)
//    cross-reference. Neither neighbour's package was edited from this
//    side.
//
// STAGE 2 (DECISION-0379 with deontics, 26.09.2026; status implemented_unverified, not reviewed):
// every remaining disposition of sections 6103, 6104, 6105 and 6110 is classified in
// docs/foundations/us-irc/coverage/confidentiality.json (930 rows). New modules:
//   09 permission vocabulary (recipient classes, generic request facts, the named organs);
//   10 §6103(d)(2)-(6) State audit agencies / death-information contract bar / regional agencies;
//   11 §6103(e) material-interest remainder (incl. the (e)(8)-(9) duties and the (e)(10) limit);
//   12 §6103(f)(2)-(5), (g), (h) committees, President, Treasury, Justice, proceedings;
//   13 §6103(i) criminal, terrorism, fugitives, Comptroller General (court-order POWERS);
//   14 §6103(j), (k), (m), (n), (o) statistical use, tax administration, addresses, others;
//   15 §6103(l) non-tax purposes (Social Security, child support, education, Medicare, ...);
//   16 §6103(p) remainder and (q) procedure, reports, State attachments, contractors;
//   17 §6104(a)-(c), (d)(3),(5)-(8) public inspection and State officials;
//   18 §6110(b)(3), (d)-(m) third-party contacts, actions, postponements, Chief Counsel advice,
//      civil remedies, fees, disposal, precedent, exclusions.
// Modelling rule of the stage: a permission is a defeater of the §6103(a) prohibition through
// `disclosure_permitted`; "shall furnish/disclose" is a duty of the discloser with the requester
// as beneficiary; use and redisclosure limits are prohibitions of the recipient; court orders,
// petitions, extensions and civil actions are powers with their statutory windows; what a
// duty does not require is a liberty to withhold. Technical gaps: G3400-G3403 (TECH-GAPS.md).
// Stage-1 edits made in stage 2: module 02 (d)(1) rule gets the (d)(4) bar defeater; module 08
// (a) rule gets the (l) exclusion defeater and the "if later" helper is defeasible; three stage-1
// scenarios corrected (see HANDOFF).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.confidentiality version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:confidentiality:clir";

import us.irc.core version "0.1.1";

type Person = us.irc.core::Person;
type Individual = us.irc.core::Individual;
type Corporation = us.irc.core::Corporation;
type Partnership = us.irc.core::Partnership;
type Trust = us.irc.core::Trust;
type Estate = us.irc.core::Estate;
type Organ = us.irc.core::Organ;
type TaxableYear = us.irc.core::TaxableYear;
type Return = us.irc.core::Return;
type Assessment = us.irc.core::Assessment;

const Secretary: Organ = us.irc.core::Secretary;
const Congress: Organ = us.irc.core::Congress;
const TaxCourt: Organ = us.irc.core::TaxCourt;
const DistrictCourt: Organ = us.irc.core::DistrictCourt;
const IRS: Organ = us.irc.core::IRS;
